    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on speed-centric upside, led by **Corbin Carroll** (76.14) and **Mickey Moniak** (72.73). **Corbin Carroll** profiles as our premier play against McDonald; his base projection is bolstered by an advantageous platoon split and a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher that creates an elite environment for his stolen base prowess. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+14%) despite facing a tough arm in Meyer, highlighting the system\u2019s tendency to chase high-environment outcomes over raw SP quality. **James Wood** also earns a strong recommendation (63.21) as he continues to display elite xwOBA metrics, with the leadoff spot providing the necessary volume to capitalize on his speed.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Edwin Arroyo** (38.31), who sat just shy of our 40-point efficiency floor. While his switch-hitting ability offers versatility, the combination of a difficult matchup against the lefty Drohan and a suppressed batting order slot (9th) dragged his score down, ultimately making him an easy exclusion in favor of our higher-upside starters. We are currently navigating a significant injury drain with **Trevor Story** and **Giancarlo Stanton** sidelined, forcing reliance on middle-of-the-order pieces like **Austin Riley** and **Seiya Suzuki** to stabilize the lineup. Managers should monitor **Jose Caballero** and **Kyle Karros**, both of whom are batting 8th; while **Jose Caballero** provides necessary SB depth, his score is depressed by a significant platoon disadvantage, making them the most volatile spots in our daily construction.",
